export anchor RadarStyle:
    number: 307
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Radar
    idea: An air traffic radar scope where services are blips on healthy, degraded and outage rings under a sweeping wedge, with flight progress strips, phosphor traces, advisories and departures beside it.
    base: dark
    palette:
        scopeBlack: #020a06, the page and style sheet
        scopeFace: #03140b, the scope centre and trace panels
        strip: #0a1f13, service strips
        ring: #1d5a37, rings, borders and rules
        phosphor: #7dffb0, healthy blips, headings, the traffic trace and the primary button
        ink: #d6ffe6, body text
        muted: #6fc796, labels and axes
        amber: #ffc94a, Degraded, the incident box and p95
        sky: #8fd8ff, Recovered and p50
        coral: #ff8a7a, the error trace and Firing
        focus: #ffffff, a dashed white focus outline
    type:
        Monospace throughout, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas,
        DejaVu Sans Mono, at 14px and 1.5. Strip names 17px bold, the
        incident number 20px bold amber, section titles 13px bold caps
        tracked 0.14em in phosphor, strip labels 11px caps, blip names 15px
        bold inside the scope.
    layout:
        A header holds a small radar mark, BRIGHTWORK OPS, the apps as
        plain links with Ops underlined, and Sector production window 24 h.
        The top area pairs a 560px circular scope with a column of strips.
        The scope has a bezel ring, three rings for healthy, degraded and
        outage labelled along the right axis, cross hairs, degree ticks and
        a static conic sweep wedge. Each service is its status shape used
        as a blip, api, web and notifications on the inner ring,
        sync-worker on the middle ring and billing on the outer ring, each
        named with its word beside it. A caption and a shape key sit under
        the scope. The column holds five flight strips, each with a 10px
        coloured tab, the name, status and uptime with metric in dashed
        cells, then the incident as an amber box. Below run three phosphor
        trace panels for traffic, errors and latency with notes, then
        Advisories for alerts and Departures for deploys as ruled rows.
        Below 1000px the scope sits above the strips, and at phone width
        only blip names show in the scope and strips wrap to two rows.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between scope, strips and traces, 6px between strips.
    density: Medium. The scope dominates, the strips are compact.
    corners: A circular scope, square strips, 8px trace panels, round buttons.
    borders: 1px #1d5a37 rings and panels, dashed dividers inside strips, an amber border on the incident.
    shadows: An 8px bezel ring around the scope and a soft phosphor glow on traces.
    icons:
        The status shapes are the blips themselves, a ringed tick for
        Healthy, a triangle for Degraded and a circular arrow for
        Recovered, and they repeat beside every status word, with a bolt
        for Firing, a tick for Resolved and a magnifier for Investigating.
    focus: A 2px dashed white outline offset 3px.
    tone: Air traffic words kept plain, such as Sector, Service strips, Advisories and Departures.
